== step 3: the kernel's own local elasticity. Design and predictions, before any kernel run ==

Design (fixed now). 12 inputs: one per L ∈ {100, 500, 1000} and ω range [0.3, 0.6), [0.6, 1),
[1, 1.5), [1.5, 2.2), drawn near the table's boundary by mode `select` (seed 20261120 + 10·(index
of L) + range; phase B's inputs excluded). Arms ω·e^{−0.2} and ω·e^{+0.2} (a factor 1.49 between
them), all other inputs fixed. Kernel: `equilibrium_world` with a burn-in of 1000 generations
before the move (not the protocol's 10,000 from zero: cost; validate/init_equilibrium.jl found
100–1000 generations enough at 100–1000 loci outside the Gaussian regime; the kernel's V_G at the
move is checked below against the table's column for the same input), move at 10000, alive =
completes generation 11999 (the table's T > 2000). Pilot at the input's own ω: 11 rates = the table
model's k50 × exp(−0.75:0.15:0.75), 6 runs each; then 8 rates = pilot k50 × exp(±0.04, ±0.12,
±0.20, ±0.28), 30 runs per rate and arm, the same seeds in both arms. Estimate: Spearman–Kärber
mean of log k50 per arm, e = Δ log k50/0.4, paired bootstrap CI; a logistic fit as comparator. An
arm whose lowest rate has < 80% alive or whose highest has > 20% alive is flagged (and may be
extended, reported as such). Emulators over the same arms: the screen at ω−, ω, ω+ (all 12), the
same closure on the grid (inputs 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11) and default :spectrum (5, 7, 9, 11) — the
grid closures on a subset because step 2b cost 0.4 CPU-h more than planned (decided before any of
them is run); :rare_alleles on all.

Predictions:
 K1. The kernel's local e_ω is negative in all 12 inputs and far from the tercile value: pooled
     −0.35 to −0.5 (the table's sub-range fits say −0.51, −0.42, −0.37 for L = 100, 500, 1000). If
     instead the kernel gave about −0.17, T would be wrong and the table's sub-range fits misleading.
 K2. The screen's finite difference over the same arms is more negative than the kernel's by about
     0.05 at L = 100 and 0.1–0.2 at L = 500 and 1000 (step 2a's residual), i.e. the screen is
     modestly too sensitive; the difference is within the kernel's CI for most single inputs.
 K3. Level: screen k50 / kernel k50 above 1.15 at L ≥ 500 for ω < 0.75 and larger at ω− than at
     ω+ (that is what an excess sensitivity means); 0.85–1.1 at L = 100.
 K4. Beta against grid: the same finite difference within 0.03. Default :spectrum (no LD): k50
     higher than the screen's, elasticity within 0.1 of the screen's.
