Reading of step 4 (after seeing it):
 - L1 HOLDS; E-3 is REJECTED. In the kernel the realised response of the mean genotype is
   0.994–1.004 of V_G·λ/S and the mean fitness 0.999–1.000 of the Gaussian formula with QTSim's
   constant, at both arms of all 12 inputs, including ω− = 0.29–0.44 where ω² is 3–10× V_P.
 - Levels under the move. At L = 100 the screen's V_G is within about ±25% of the kernel's and
   early in the move too LOW (0.65–0.83 at 50–350 generations in inputs 1 and 2); the screen then
   dies at ω+ in inputs 1, 2 and 4 at a rate at which all kernel runs live (its k50 is 11–26% too
   low at L = 100, step 3b). At L ≥ 500 the screen's V_G is right for the first 100–150 generations
   (0.99–1.16) and then too HIGH: 1.18–1.63 at 250–350, 1.20–1.80 at 900–1100, in all 8 inputs.
   The kernel's V_G declines under the move and the screen's much less; default :spectrum (no LD)
   is 1.2–4.8× the kernel's. This is the decline of validate/genic_decline.md, not a new finding.
 - L2 is NOT SUPPORTED as stated. In the five inputs with an excess sensitivity the ratio
   screen/kernel V_G at 250–1100 generations does not fall from ω− to ω+: it is equal in 7 and 8
   (1.25/1.28, 1.20/1.20; 1.25/1.24, 1.28/1.28), rises in 10 and 11 (1.61→1.80, 1.50→1.78 at
   900–1100) and falls only in 12 (1.57→1.39). The inputs without an excess (5, 6, 9) show the
   same level error (1.39–1.65). So at a COMMON rate the screen's error in V_G under the move is of
   the same size in both arms; this comparison does not show why the screen's k50 loses its
   excess with ω in 7, 8, 10, 11, 12 and not in 5, 6, 9.
   Caveat on the design (seen only now): one common rate puts the two arms at different distances
   from their own thresholds (ω+ at 0.85 k50, ω− at about 0.72–0.78 k50), and near the threshold
   V_G and the lag are not stationary within the horizon (inputs 7, 8, 10, 11, 12 at ω+: the
   kernel's lag still grows and V_G still falls at 1700–1999), so death within 2000 generations is
   a race between the erosion of V_G and the horizon, not a steady state. A comparison at equal
   relative distance from each arm's k50 was not run (budget).
 - L3 / E-4: the kernel's survival is a step in the rate (logistic width 0.008–0.031 in log k per
   input; step 3a), i.e. deaths are a deterministic runaway as in validate/spectrum_diagnosis.md,
   so there is no sign that between-run variance or the binomial extinction link matters here; it
   was not tested further.
 - By elimination (state at the move right: steps 2b, 3b; Gaussian response and mean fitness
   exact: L1; extinction a deterministic runaway), the residual excess sensitivity of the screen at
   L ≥ 500 has to sit in the course of V_G under the move, where the screen is known to be wrong
   in level; its dependence on ω is not isolated.
 - Not run: the block-lineage model over the same ±δ (budget: 5.44 CPU-h used by clock()).

